/** \page release_notes Revision History

\section rev_3_7 Revision 3.7
  - Functional changes.
    - None.
  - Cosmetic and non-functional changes.
    - Reworking of development flow to allow reuse with other applications.
  - Performance changes.
    - None.
  - Bug fixes.
    - None.

\section rev_3_6_17 Revision 3.6.17
- Functional changes.
  - Add feature to display previous QSO records with contact in log table.
  - When comparing a download, show differing records first after essential fields.
  - When deleting a record, park it in a deleted records table for possible later recovery.
  - Add feature to select different bands in the band-plan viewer.
  - Add scratchpad for recording notes and pasting data into QSO records.
  - Change contest algorithm definition to use files rather than hard-coded algorithms.
- Cosmetic and non-functional changes.
  - Moved more non-ZZALOG code to ZZACOMMON.
  - Remove requirement for user to interact with ZZACOMMON during build flow.
- Performance changes.
  - None.
- Bug fixes.
  - None.

\section rev_3_6_16 Revision 3.6.16

- Functional changes.
  - Add command line option -h [html|pdf] to open HTML or PDF userguide.
  - Add command line debug switch -d s to display status messages on terminal.
  - Inhibit auto power-down with -o switch.
- Cosmetic and non-functional changes.
  - Remove or reword typos and unhelpful information in status messages.
  - Remove -g command line switch as no longer does anything.
  - Moved more non-ZZALOG code to ZZACOMMON.
  - In cold-start dialogs, make the required fields more obvious.
  - Include ADIF 3.1.7.
- Performance changes.
  - None.
- Bug fixes.
  - In Windows, after starting another app, the batch script window is not closed
  when ZZALOG is closed.
  - Clicking more than once on a QSL download buttons may cause lock up.
  - Occasional exception when closing ZZALOG: probable race hazard while closing ticker.
  - Command line switches after debug switches wrongly regarded as bad debug switches.
  - Cold start deletes an existing file if it is selected as the logbook file.
  - DLLs missing from Windows release build.
  
\section rev_3_6_15 Revision 3.6.15

- Functional changes.
  - Add feature to configure the font in which status messages are displayed.
  - Restore original FlLog emulation (removed in 3.6.12) after bug fixes therewith.
  - Add QTH in QSO record as source of location data, looking up in openweather.org.
  - Add mirroring of logbook file to support use of network files.
  - Cold start: require minimum amount of user data.
  - Add feature to power the rigs down.
- Cosmetic and non-functional changes.
  - Prevent banner from always appearing on top of dashboard.
  - Remove cursor manipulation.
  - Allow terminal-style monospace font for log tables.
  - Change presentation in qso_dxcc pane: describe source of latitude and longitude more clearly.
  - Add LGPL licence.
  - Separate API documentation for ZZALOG and ZZACOMMON.
- Performance changes.
  - None.
- Bug fixes.
  - Improve resilience to FlRig status when launching ZZALOG
  with auto-start feature enabled. 
  - Country data file timestamps not recorded correctly.
  - Spurious updates to QSO records with non-critical data.
  - Callsign decode partly left displayed when QSO not selected.
  - Correct or remove misleading messages.

\subpage rev_3_6


*/